From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:22:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: end a rest when the voltage
 moves

A rest reading pairs the voltage now with the current of the last
counter window. When a charge or a load starts between that window and
the read, the voltage already carries the new current while the window
still reads idle. On station-work-110, a battery resting at 44 %
started charging when a charge limit was lifted, and the next read took
the charging voltage as an OCV: capacity jumped to 76 %, and counted on
from there.

A rested cell's voltage moves a few mV over seconds. If the voltage is
more than 25 mV from the last window's closing voltage, the rest is
over: take no rest reading, end the rest, and keep counting.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index ffdad4c..140d12a 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -56,6 +56,12 @@
 
 /* Inside the idle current for this long, the voltage is taken as the OCV. */
 #define MT6351_FG_REST_MS		(300 * MSEC_PER_SEC)
+/*
+ * A rested cell's voltage moves a few mV over seconds: a reading this far from
+ * the last window's closing voltage means a load or a charge started since that
+ * window, so the rest is over and no rest reading is taken.
+ */
+#define MT6351_FG_REST_DV_UV		25000
 
 /*
  * Learning the full charge: two OCV readings, each after this long a rest,
@@ -678,6 +684,14 @@ static int mt6351_fg_capacity(struct mt6351_fg *fg, int ua, int *capacity,
 			ret = thermal_zone_get_temp(fg->tz, &mc);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
+		/* The current is from the last window: check the rest still holds. */
+		if (settled && fg->win_prev_valid &&
+		    abs(uv - fg->win_prev_uv) > MT6351_FG_REST_DV_UV) {
+			dev_dbg(fg->dev, "rest ended: %d uV after %d uV\n", uv, fg->win_prev_uv);
+			fg->resting = false;
+			fg->full_rest = false;
+			goto counted;
+		}
 		/* The open-circuit voltage: charging current raises the terminal. */
 		uv = mt6351_fg_ocv(fg, uv, ua, mc);
 		ret = power_supply_batinfo_ocv2cap(fg->info, uv, mc / 1000);
@@ -755,6 +769,7 @@ static int mt6351_fg_capacity(struct mt6351_fg *fg, int ua, int *capacity,
 		}
 	}
 
+counted:
 	if (mt6351_fg_learn_r(fg, now, ua, full))
 		*full_changed = true;
 
